Intended use
------------
This map is intended to use with Bacteriochlorophyll c (bChl-c) molecules (all-atom models only!). It provides the electronic excitation energy and corresponding energy fluctuation due to changes in the molecule's electrostatic environment.

How to use
----------
This map has no specific requirements beyond the availability of the bChl-c electrostatic environment
There exists a file "main_MG_position.py" which can be renamed to "main.py" in order to use the positions of the Magnesium atoms when making the electrostatic cut-off, rather than the centre of mass positions. This MG reference position was used to determine the chlorosome spectrum in the published work.

If one wants to apply this map to united-atom models, the difference charges file needs to be edited such that the difference charge of a hydrogen atom is added to the atom it is bound to. Of course, all other files need to be changed accordingly, too.

Available parameters
--------------------
At this point the map has no additional parameters available.

Warnings that can be raised by this map
---------------------------------------
At this point none